": "solved", "failure_reason": null, "faults_served": 0, "final_answer_complete": true, "final_answer_present": true, "final_answer_source": "stdout", "first_after_build": false, "first_side": "without", "fresh_subagents": 0, "harness": "opencode", "harness_version": "0.0.0--202610170413 (/workspace/openbench-ab/results/opencode-src/bin/e3471526f4c71b2c4ee00117e125e179da01e6e2/opencode)", "harness_version_source": "host", "host": "grok-bot-vm-412615941", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": true, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": null, "model_max_tokens": null, "output_tail": "[tool: read]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: bash]\nThe read tool errored on the directory (it can't list directories and returned a confusing \"did you mean\" pointing at the same path). I'll use glob to list the files instead.\n[tool: glob]\n[tool: bash]\nReading all source and test files.\n[tool: bash]\nApplying the fixes:\n[tool: read]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: bash]\nAll 16 tests pass now. Before the fix, 15 ran: the search tests couldn't be imported, so they weren't counted.\n\n**The three reads you asked for:**\n- **(a)** Reading the `catalog/` directory with the read tool failed. It returned \"File not found\" and then suggested the same path back as \"Did you mean\u2026\". So the read tool doesn't list directories, even though the error message implies the path is wrong. I used glob to list the files instead.\n- **(b)** Offset 0, limit 5 returned lines 1\u20135 of `books.py`.\n- **(c)** Offset 3, limit 5 returned lines 4\u20138, not 3\u20137. The tool's description says the offset is 0-based, which fits: offset 3 skips three lines. But the output labels lines starting from 1, so the numbers shown are one higher than the offset you pass.\n\n**Fixes, all in `catalog/`; no tests changed:**\n- `books.py:22`: `parse_book` now turns the year into an `int`. It was being kept as a string, which broke `age()`.\n- `factory.py`: added the missing `Emma` book, which the docstring already says should be there.\n- `fees.py:14`: the fee was `days_late + DAILY_FEE`; it's now `days_late * DAILY_FEE`.\n- `inventory.py`: `recent(n)` was off by one and returned `n+1` events. It now returns the last `n`, and an empty list when `n <= 0`.\n- `members.py:4`: changed `MAX_BORROWED` from 3 to 5 to match the five-book limit in the comment and the tests.\n- `search.py:3`: `normalize` was imported from a module that doesn't exist; it now comes from `catalog.text`.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "params_stripped": ["param:temperature"], "params_stripped_requests": 1, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 8, "replies_ok": null, "replies_throttled": null, "requests_cache_read": 95808, "requests_cache_write": 63052, "requests_cost_usd": 0.39374159999999997, "requests_count": 8, "requests_input_uncached": 20, "requests_output": 2962, "reread": true, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "opencode:trig-read-edge:claude-opus-5-5:trial6", "run_seed": 1016, "sampling_observed": null, "schedule_index": 250, "score": 1.0, "started_at": "2026-10-18T07:26:21.781388+00:00", "subagent_resumed": false, "subagent_write_calls": 0, "success": true, "t_agent_s": 35.363, "t_checker_s": 0.175, "t_env_setup_s": 0.001, "task": "trig-read-edge", "task_calls": 0, "thinking_mode": "default", "thinking_sent": ["none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none"], "timeout_s": 840, "tmpdir_leaked_dirs": 0, "token_basis": "proxy_measured", "token_basis_main": "vendor_split", "token_basis_proxy": "proxy_measured", "tokens": 2982, "tokens_cache_read": 95808, "tokens_cache_write": 63052, "tokens_fresh": 2964, "tokens_input_uncached": 20, "tokens_main_cache_read": 94776, "tokens_main_cache_write": 63052, "tokens_main_calls": 7, "tokens_main_input_uncached": 16, "tokens_main_output": 2948, 